      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metekhi_church_in_Tbilisi._View_from_the_south-west._December_2023.jpg",
        "author": "Kober",
        "date": "2023-12-03",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Entire500x667 ordinary southwest view inspected. Compact warm patched stone cross-domed church, intersecting gables, small narrow body/gable windows, arcaded drum and grey standing-seam conical roof/cross. Church stands above a steep natural river cliff and separate terrace/wall; cliff, river and terrace remain host context."
      },
      {
        "page": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metekhi_church,_view_from_the_north._Tbilisi,_Georgia._July_2023.jpg",
        "author": "Kober",
        "date": "2023-07-02",
        "license": "CC0-1.0",
        "inspected": true,
        "observations": "Entire500x572 ordinary north view inspected to fill porch coverage gap. Projecting gabled north porch, large pointed side arch/recessed layered archivolts, two small front arched windows, brick gable patch/raised brick base and stone/brick cornices. Main north gable and narrow upper window behind it. Opposite porch side and exact masonry inventory remain approximate."
      }
    ],
    "scope": "Specific standing Metekhi church: mapped stone body with intersecting gables, three projecting eastern apses and metal cap roofs, twelve-sided drum with narrow real window apertures/blind arched surrounds, grey conical standing-seam roof and metal cross. Projecting north porch has a gabled brick/stone front, real pointed side arches, two narrow front windows and a recessed timber church entrance. Shared ashlar/brick/metal textures, original simplified archivolts/lozenge relief and short local approaches. Natural cliff, terrace, river, monument and independent buildings remain host context. No full ritual interior or copied inscription/stone inventory."
